  "reason": "Evidence: Our three completed experiments show that (1) image-only (ViT-L, singleprofile) is weak (0.227 acc), (2) RNA-only (scgpt, singleprofile) is moderate (0.411 acc), and (3) multimodal (scgpt + ViT-L, singleprofile, weighted) gives a small lift over RNA alone (0.422 vs 0.411). The marginal multimodal gain suggests the current singleprofile representation may be a bottleneck for both modalities. Uncertainty: We have zero data on whether multiprofile with aggregation can unlock additional signal that singleprofile cannot capture. This is the largest unexplored design axis. Question: Does moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with transformer aggregation improve performance, holding encoders (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l) and fusion (weighted) constant? Why this is the best next experiment: config_010 is the minimal, logical extension of our best result (config_012), changing only the profile/aggregation axis. If it helps, we confirm the profile bottleneck and can further optimize aggregation; if it does not, we rule out that axis and redirect budget toward encoder or fusion choices. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most impactful untested design decision under our limited budget."
}

